From: nuubOS Project <noreply@nuubos.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] video: nuubOS square picture fills a square screen

In smart integer scaling a 1:1 picture on a 1:1 screen is scaled to
fill it instead of the largest integer factor: PICO-8 (128x128) on the
RG CubeXX (720x720) was 640x640 in a 40-pixel frame. nuubOS draws
non-integer scales with a sharp bilinear preset. Every other shape, and
square pictures on other screens, keep the integer rule.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [nuubOS specific]
---
--- a/gfx/video_driver.c
+++ b/gfx/video_driver.c
@@ -2859,7 +2859,14 @@
              * TODO: Make this threshold configurable. */
             float width_utilization  = (float)(width  - padding_x) / width;
             float height_utilization = (float)(height - padding_y) / height;
-            if (MAX(height_utilization, width_utilization) < 0.88)
+            /* nuubOS: a square picture on a square screen (PICO-8 on the
+             * RG CubeXX's 720x720) fills it: integer 5x left a 40-pixel
+             * frame; the sharp bilinear preset keeps a fractional scale
+             * even. Other shapes keep the integer rule. */
+            bool nuubos_square = abs((int)width - (int)height) <= (int)height / 100
+                  && fabsf(aspect_ratio - 1.0f) < 0.01f;
+            if (MAX(height_utilization, width_utilization) < 0.88
+                  || (nuubos_square && (padding_x > 0 || padding_y > 0)))
             {
                video_viewport_get_scaled_aspect(vp, width, height, y_down);
                return;
